 {
  "type": "text",
  "id": "kds-tips",
  "x": 5594,
  "y": -9780,
  "width": 167,
  "height": 20,
  "text": "- Exam Tips & Traps",
  "fontSize": 16
 },
 {
  "type": "text",
  "id": "kds-tipst",
  "x": 5609,
  "y": -9752,
  "width": 612,
  "height": 42,
  "text": "1. KDS = you run the consumers and can replay. Firehose = fully managed delivery to S3/Redshift/OpenSearch, no replay.\n2. ProvisionedThroughputExceeded: spread the partition key, add shards (split), or switch to on-demand.\n3. Many consumers on one stream with low latency: enhanced fan-out. Poison record in Lambda: bisect batch + on-failure destination.\n4. Kafka API or existing Kafka clients: Amazon MSK. Stateful windows/joins on the stream: Managed Service for Apache Flink.",
  "fontSize": 8.5
 }
]